.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
node_modules/
.env
.env.local

# Tool caches (serena local index; the kit uses codebase-memory, not serena)
.serena/

# Local Claude Code user state and per-machine settings, except the ROOT
# repo memory (git-tracked by design so it rides the repo, per CLAUDE.md).
# Four patterns because of two gitignore rules: a directory-match excludes
# the whole subtree from traversal (so no nested negation can apply), and a
# later pattern overrides an earlier one. Line 1 ignores every .claude/ dir
# at any depth (megagoal archives etc.); line 2 re-includes the root one so
# git traverses it; line 3 re-ignores its children; line 4 exempts memory.
**/.claude/
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/memory/

# Legacy / retired artifacts the kit no longer writes: review output now lives in
# the spec's `## Review` section, and the spec location unified onto docs/specs/
# (ADR-0010). Kept ignored so a stray copy (an older kit version, a downstream
# project, or a manual run) can never slip into version control.
REVIEW.md
TODOS.md
.planning/

# Wavefront/orchestrator runtime artifacts (SPEC-106 TASK-008). A mega-goal run writes
# per-edge handoffs, the event log / per-session logs / stream captures, and the flip lock
# into its mega-goal dir; session logs + stream json can carry resolved op:// values, and
# the per-edge handoffs multiply the surface. Never commit them. (`.claude/worktrees/` is
# already covered by the `.claude/` rule above.)
# LOCATION-INDEPENDENT: `orchestrate.sh run <dir>` accepts ANY megadir (the "promote to
# project" workflow moves a live mega-goal to `<repo>/projects/<slug>/`), so these must NOT
# be scoped to `_meta/megagoals/**` or a promoted megadir's handoffs leak (security review).
HANDOFF*.md
**/.orchestrate/
*.session.log
*.stream.jsonl

# Python bytecode caches (e.g. lib/handoff/__pycache__) , regenerated, never tracked.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# install.sh's per-consumer module manifest (ID-277 SG-04). Only meaningful at an
# INSTALLED destination; an in-place install (KIT_DIR == ~/.claude/dwarves-kit) writes
# it at the repo root, so it must never be committed from a maintainer's own machine.
/kit.toml

# Rust build output anywhere in lib/ (a branch without a module's own .gitignore
# must still never sweep another branch's build artifacts into git add -A)
lib/**/rust/target/
lib/**/bin/*-rs
.coverage

# Operator-local install state when ~/.claude/dwarves-kit is a symlink to this clone (dev-machine layout, 2026-09-08).
state/
logs/
INSTALL-STAMP
